  "marks": "Mastering (7-8): Considers all four combinations (high carbon steel for gear, high carbon steel for bus bar, copper for gear, copper for bus bar). High carbon steel: high hardness after quenching — excellent for gear (resists wear from mesh contact); poor conductor — unsuitable for bus bar. Copper: excellent electrical and thermal conductor — ideal for bus bar; low hardness and ductile — will wear quickly at gear mesh contact, so unsuitable. Conclusion identifies that neither metal performs well in both roles — each must be matched to the application it suits. Response is structured as an evaluation, not a list.\nSecure (5-6): Both metals evaluated against at least two requirements; conclusion present but may not consider all four combinations.\nDeveloping (3-4): Each metal given one relevant property; limited cross-comparison.\nEmerging (1-2): One metal addressed or properties listed without application links."
 }
]

