  "definition": "Shaping a metal at room temperature by rolling, pressing or drawing, which increases its hardness and strength but reduces its ductility."
 },
 {
  "term": "quenching",
  "definition": "Heating a high-carbon steel to above its critical temperature and then cooling it very rapidly (usually in water or oil) to trap a hard, brittle crystal structure called martensite."
 }
]


